00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:33.650
The Brazilian government has blamed deliberate human action for a wave of fires in Amazonas

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:33.990
state.

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:40.590
The National Institute for Space Research, Brazil's satellite monitoring body, recorded 540 new

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.150
hot spots in 48 hours.

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:45.970
A state of emergency has been declared in 36 municipalities.

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:50.770
Officials link the fires to illegal clearing and land use practices that have increased

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:51.350
this year.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:56.650
The satellite data showed that 48-hour total exceeded half of all hot spots detected

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:58.350
throughout October 2025.

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:03.130
Environmental groups have called for stronger enforcement against those starting the fires.

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:07.910
Local authorities are coordinating emergency responses across the affected areas.

